# ARCHITECTURE.md §3 marks BOTH of these untracked.
#
# This departs from Corner, which deliberately tracks design/ on the argument
# that small diffable design output earns its history. The spec says untracked,
# so untracked it is — see CONVENTIONS.md §10, departure 2.
#
# Both directories keep an on-disk README.md that is NOT committed. Do not add a
# !marketing/README.md or !design/README.md negation to force them into the
# index; those files are meant to live on disk for humans only.
marketing/
design/

*.log
.DS_Store
.worktrees/
worktrees/

# KEPT ON DISK, DELIBERATELY OUT OF THE REMOTE.
#
# The GitHub repo is public. None of these is needed to build or run the
# service — they are the product, not the code. The spec carries pricing and
# positioning, DEFERRED carries the unit economics and the open decisions, and
# RETRIEVAL-HARM is an incident write-up. Losing them would hurt; publishing
# them would hurt more, and a public push cannot be taken back.
#
# If the repo is ever made private, delete this block — these belong in history.
/ARCHITECTURE.md
/DEFERRED.md
/docs/

# ABIGAIL'S PROMPTS. The service will not boot without them.
#
# The code that uses these ships; the text does not. They are NOT generated and
# NOT reconstructable from this repository — if the working copy is lost, they
# are lost. Back them up somewhere that is not this machine and not this repo.
# See discern-backend/src/config/prompts.ts.
/prompts/
